    "conclusion": "Empirical profiling establishes a peak resident set size of 1369.79 MB for BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T (i2_s) and 1523.52 MB for the 270M embedder. Compared against the published Gemma 2 2B FP16 baseline footprint of 5400.0 MB, 1.58-bit quantization reduces memory overhead by a factor of 3.94x. Under 4-thread CPU execution, BitNet achieves 19.49 tokens/second decode throughput, 114.47 tokens/second prefill throughput, and a time-to-first-token of 244.6 ms."
